 "goldenFixtureFix": "STEP_ORDER (config.ts) now dispatches only retrieve/analyze/decide/review; `event_card_build` (and every other producer step) is no longer a valid --stop-after target, so both of fixture-deterministic.test.ts's beforeAll blocks (main describe, 14 tests; 'extract firewall regression' describe, 5 tests) threw immediately and all 19 tests were vitest-skipped as a side effect of the failed suite. I rewrote the main describe block to drive `runPipeline` directly (not the old run-fixture.ts cache-seed harness, which is extract/classify-cache-specific and has nothing left to seed): ingest goes through the REAL feedq adapter via a fake `npx tsx` script that echoes the tiny fixture's real 5-article articles.json (so feed-trace.json/step-trace-ingest.json get one genuine traced call, not an injected-source vacuous pass), and retrieve/analyze/decide/review are replaced with `stepRunners` \u2014 the exact deterministic-injection mechanism `pipeline-run-modes.test.ts` already uses for the same purpose (no LLM, no cache, no seed file needed at all). The fake step outputs honestly cite two distinct REAL article_refs from the fixture. New assertions cover exactly the five things the task asked for: STEP_ORDER's four steps all ran in order; analyze scenarios/factor_views and decide target_positions carry non-empty source_refs; feed-trace.json + step-trace-ingest.json exist, reconcile byte-for-byte (sha256 + byte_size) against every entry in the artifacts.json manifest, and the traced call's own feed-calls payload file is present and correct; citation-lint (lintCitations for analyze/decide, lintVerbatimQuotes for retrieve) passes against a freshly rebuilt trace-backed source_ref universe, with a mutation-proof (a fabricated ref is still rejected) so the pass isn't vacuous; and run-summary stage_status is 'ok' for all four consumer steps, plus a bonus non-zero retrieval_quality.themes_total assertion (using an explicitly-supplied quality_verdict in the fake retri